newJitIfT -- SEQ 525 (S3 of docs/jitterWalkRecon.md): ifThen through the jit brackets. Run plain (the twin, testOP) and with jitter;
after the last ifNew. i1 / i2 each arm by value; i3 / i4 no else, each way; i5 a nested if in a seq arm; i6 an or chain; i7 a seq
arm with a handed-over print in it, native on both sides; i8 / ih return in an arm, taken (nothing after it prints; IF ig reads 9 at the top level) and not taken (a compiled arm's fallback leaves through the epilogue);
i9 / ia / ie conditions that hand the whole if over (&&, a string, a bare read); ib a number crossing the compare; ic a break in a
single-statement arm (the action's seq catches it, so the action ends); id a break in a seq arm (that seq catches it, so the statement
after the if still runs: the whole if hands over until S4).
